routing.lifecycle-campaign-tagging-steward:
# AGENTS

When the measurement is trustworthy again and the revenue ranking can be finished:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please re-run the per-flow revenue read on the corrected tagging.

When the disagreement turns out to be an attribution window rather than a tagging fault:
  @Churn and Win-Back Analyst, please tell me which window your recovery numbers assume.

routing.lifecycle-churn-analyst:
# AGENTS

When the intervention is designed and needs building as a flow:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please specify the trigger, exclusions and timing for this sequence.

When a risk signal exists in the events but is not readable on the profile:
  @Customer Event Schema Engineer, please flatten or sync the property so the segment can be built.

routing.lifecycle-event-schema-engineer:
# AGENTS

When the schema fix has landed and the blocked flow can be specified:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please write the build specification for the flow this unblocks.

When a property gap is blocking a risk signal rather than a flow:
  @Churn and Win-Back Analyst, please confirm which signal you need on the profile and at what refresh rate.

routing.lifecycle-flow-auditor:
# AGENTS

When a recommended flow cannot be built because the segment it needs has no reachable property:
  @Customer Event Schema Engineer, please map the property and specify the smallest schema change that unblocks it.

When the gap is a retention gap rather than a missing message:
  @Churn and Win-Back Analyst, please size the leaving and design the intervention that matches the cause.

When two reports disagree about what the programme earned:
  @Campaign Tagging Steward, please audit the tagging and reconcile the numbers before I rank anything on them.
